Adding `"aiter"` to `DSA_FP8_COMPATIBLE_DECODE_IMPLS` removes the only skip this helper had for AITER. `test_dsa.py` is registered on `4-gpu-b200` and `1-gpu-large`, so `test_sparse_fp8_decode_cases[impl=aiter]` now reaches `_forward_aiter` on CUDA and hits `self.need_pad_heads`, which is only set under `_is_hip` → `AttributeError`. Please gate on `dsa_impl_capability` first, as `run_dsa_sparse_decode_impl_variant_case` does:

```suggestion
    supported, reason = dsa_impl_capability(dsa_decode_backend)
    if not supported:
        testcase.skipTest(
            f"DSA decode impl `{dsa_decode_backend}` not supported: {reason}"
        )
    if dsa_decode_backend not in DSA_FP8_COMPATIBLE_DECODE_IMPLS:
```

